## What Changed

All advisory skills renamed for clarity. Advisors are auto-triggered behavioral rules, not user-invocable commands.

| Old Name | New Name | New Type |
|----------|----------|----------|
| `wai-lug-advisor.md` | `wai-lug-schema.md` | guard |
| `wai-complexity-advisor.md` | `wai-complexity-gate.md` | guard |
| `wai-stewardship-advisor.md` | `wai-stewardship-guard.md` | guard |
| `wai-context-advisor.md` | `wai-context-guard.md` | guard |
| `wai-foundation-advisor.md` | `wai-foundation-gate.md` | guard |
| `wai-signal-advisor.md` | `wai-signal-capture.md` | guard |

## Why

- `-advisor` implied user-facing consultation; these are auto-triggered rules
- `-gate` = blocks until condition met (complexity, foundation)
- `-guard` = detects and flags (stewardship, context)
- `-capture` = triggers recording (signal)
- `-schema` = reference document (lug)
- Advisors should NOT appear as `/wai-*` slash commands — they are agent-internal

## Apply Instructions

1. Rename files in `WAI-Spoke/skills/`:
   - `complexity-advisor/wai-complexity-advisor.md` → `complexity-gate/wai-complexity-gate.md`
   - `stewardship-advisor/wai-stewardship-advisor.md` → `stewardship-guard/wai-stewardship-guard.md`
   - `context-advisor/wai-context-advisor.md` → `context-guard/wai-context-guard.md`
   - `foundation-advisor/wai-foundation-advisor.md` → `foundation-gate/wai-foundation-gate.md`
   - `signal-advisor/wai-signal-advisor.md` → `signal-capture/wai-signal-capture.md`
   - `lug-advisor/wai-lug-advisor.md` → `lug-schema/wai-lug-schema.md`

2. Update `WAI-Spoke/skills/WAI-Skills.jsonl` — change `id` and `command_file` for each renamed skill. Change `type` from `"advisory"` to `"guard"`.

3. Remove any `.claude/commands/wai-*-advisor.md` files (advisors/guards should not be slash commands).

4. Search-replace old names in any skill files that reference them (closeout, improve, mode, etc.).

